<title>UK: World 1996/97 cotton output revised higher.</title>
<headline>World 1996/97 cotton output revised higher.</headline>
<dateline>LIVERPOOL, England 1996-09-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Cotton Outlook revised its 1996/97 world cotton output estimate up to 19.48 million tonnes in September from the 19.46 million estimated in August.</p>
<p>In 1995/96 the total was estimated at 19.90 million tonnes.</p>
<p>U.S. output was forecast slightly lower at 4.10 against the August estimate of 4.13 million tonnes and 3.89 million in 1995/96. China's production was seen unchanged at 4 million but down on 4.77 million in 1995/96.</p>
<p>Estimates were as follows, in thousand tonnes -</p>
<p>				 1995/96		   1996/97</p>
<p>			     Sep	 Aug	 Sep	   Aug</p>
<p>Northern belt</p>
